From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:51:41 -0400
Subject: [ganesh] Handle deferred writePixels failure

When deferred texture uploads (ASAP or inline) or GrGpu::writePixels
failed, Ganesh previously ignored the return status and proceeded with
draw execution. This caused subsequent draws to sample unwritten,
recycled, or uninitialized texture memory.

This CL plumbs upload success/failure throughout the Ganesh flush
pipeline:

- Draws dependent on failed uploads are skipped during flush execution
  rather than sampling corrupt texture state.
- Backend OpsRenderPass implementations now propagate inline upload
  status instead of returning true unconditionally.
- DrawOpAtlas plots that fail to upload are cleanly evicted and reset
  so client caches are purged and plot capacity is reclaimed.
- GrOpFlushState::doUpload defensively guards against null proxies
  and surfaces to prevent crashes under OOM or context loss.

Bug: b/553130328
Change-Id: Ic9970eb327c98b94c9fb5225d1073db5a40a978b
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1369317
Commit-Queue: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Robert Phillips <robertphillips@google.com>

